<h2>No Jerseys Required</h2>
<p>I have little interest in telling people what political, philosophical, or cultural tribe they ought to belong to.</p>
<p>The world already has an impressive supply of people selling certainty by the bucket.</p>
<p>I'm more interested in whether an idea survives scrutiny, whether an institution deserves our trust, whether a belief makes us more capable of living responsibly, and whether we're willing to recognize the truth when it arrives wearing the wrong uniform.</p>
<p>I don't expect agreement.</p>
<p>In fact, thoughtful disagreement is considerably more useful than applause delivered on autopilot.</p>
<h2>The Work Continues</h2>
<p>This website isn't intended to be a finished statement about who I am or what everyone else ought to think.</p>
<p>It's a place to examine ideas, tell stories, make music, ask difficult questions, share experiments, and occasionally discover that the question itself was defective.</p>
<p>Most of the work will be serious. Some will be irreverent. Some may be deeply personal. And some will probably involve an entirely unnecessary amount of sarcasm.</p>
<p>The common thread is an attempt to remain curious without becoming gullible, principled without becoming rigid, and compassionate without surrendering judgment.</p>
<p>If something here makes you think, laugh, reconsider an assumption, or pick up a conversation you'd otherwise have avoided, then the work has done something worthwhile.</p>
<p><strong>Welcome. Have a look around. Make yourself uncomfortable enough to learn something.</strong></p>
<p><em>— Brian Reymore</em></p>
